In normal text, this is ideal: OE-Quotefix adds the obligatory > before
quoted lines, removes interspersed spaces (eg, > >text becomes >> text),
and it even fixes lines that are too long, not by just moving a single
word to the next line, but by adjusting the entire paragraph.

Also, there are options for showing emoticons instead of the ascii
smilies, stripping signatures when quoting, fixing OE's signature
delimiter error, ignoring HTML in messages, putting your signature at the
bottom instead of at the start of your reply (to prevent top-posting, and
putting your cursor at the start.

Works like a charm, and if you wish, you can turn any or all reformatting
options off. Makes OE a charm to work with. I sometimes turn it off so as
to more appreciate it afterwards...  :-)

